<p>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said a Russian missile strike on a nine-story apartment building in Kyiv killed 24 people, including three children, after emergency crews finished more than a day of search-and-rescue work in the capital’s Darnytskyi district. Ukrainian officials said 48 people were wounded in Kyiv, including two children, and city authorities declared May 15 a day of mourning. Ukraine’s air force said the strike was part of Russia’s largest aerial assault of the full-scale war, with 675 attack drones and 56 missiles launched mainly at Kyiv; Ukrainian officials said air defenses downed 652 drones and 41 missiles. Zelenskyy said Russia had launched more than 1,560 drones against Ukrainian population centers since Wednesday and that about 180 sites were damaged nationwide, including more than 50 residential buildings. The attacks followed a May 9-11 ceasefire that President Trump said he had asked Zelenskyy and Russian President Vladimir Putin to observe. Fighting continued during the 72-hour period, but at a lower scale. Russia and Ukraine also carried out a prisoner exchange of 205 captured soldiers from each side on May 15.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/riiXo1boAa0fTe3eVZUe32_dXf0PC9dpDo1Viy_OcIIajsqzR-x3MePlrTzqAdnR2vfP-1YRU9t3GxoVns-EOrn33Ow0lqqgo5T-LXAtiRMR5J1Iw2Yc1DSJ2vS4zHXYxwKUg4m6wbA5H-4ojEWplA56oxafC2j1VniPG2RgVRYjZ1NyfNuMRRXHV_FAHnO8YFap0al-RANJiJTQUCuUT3tPisZ_FGjlvw25qW2z6ZZiDZBXWzIlJKsuK9c9YmXqfa4pMc-YceCw8pFEFw' alt='Rescue workers stand in the yard of an apartment building heavily damaged after a Russian strike on a residential neighbourhood in Kyiv, Ukraine, on Friday, May 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Building collapse: Meduza reported that a section of the Darnytskyi apartment block collapsed from the first through ninth floors, destroying 18 apartments.</li><li>Regional spread: Novaya Gazeta Europe reported damage and fires in Obukhivskyi, Brovarskyi, Fastivskyi, Boryspilskyi and Bila Tserkva districts around Kyiv.</li><li>Russian air defenses: Russia’s Defense Ministry said its air defenses downed 355 Ukrainian drones overnight.</li><li>Witness account: Andriy, a Kyiv resident, told AFP near the collapsed Soviet-era residential building that everything was burning and people were screaming.</li></ul><blockquote>These are definitely not the actions of those who believe the war is coming to an end - Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy: Zelenskyy visited the damaged site, laid flowers for victims, called for more international pressure on Moscow and urged allies to strengthen Ukraine’s air defenses. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/kyiv-strike-kills-24-as-zelenskiy-condemns-russia-and-demands-global-pressure-556033/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump suggested the strike could set back efforts to negotiate an end to the war. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/trump-suggests-deadly-russian-strike-on-kyiv-could-set-back-peace-efforts'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Kyiv residents: Crowds of grieving people, many of them children, brought flowers and stuffed toys to a makeshift memorial near the destroyed building. (<a href='https://www.irishnews.com/news/world/death-toll-rises-after-attack-on-kyiv-apartment-building-MX25HBZDYZPPRJDUIFTQ63LHY4/'>Irish News</a>)</li><li>Russia: Moscow issued no immediate response to the apartment strike while maintaining its longstanding position that it does not intentionally target civilians. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/kyiv-strike-kills-24-as-zelenskiy-condemns-russia-and-demands-global-pressure-556033/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/death-toll-attack-kyiv-apartment-building-now-stands-132992721'>Death toll in attack on Kyiv apartment building now stands at 24</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ukraine-russia-launches-nonstop-aeria